<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaldean tribes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chaldean tribes were Semitic-speaking peoples who settled in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in the early first millennium BCE. They frequently resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>'s control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>. A Chaldean leader, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabopolassar">Nabopolassar</a>, founded the Neo-Babylonian or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>.</p></div>
